# Moonlight Sonata (first movement) by Ludwig van Beethoven, arranged by Claude and SZ for the
# Cinematic style: Beethoven's notes bar for bar on the grand piano, with a soft bass under the octaves.
title: Moonlight Sonata
composer: Ludwig van Beethoven
arranger: Claude & SZ
about: Beethoven's Piano Sonata No. 14, written in 1801 and dedicated to his pupil Countess Giulietta Guicciardi. The name Moonlight came decades later, from a critic who said the first movement made him think of moonlight on Lake Lucerne.
year: 1801
source: public-domain
category: classics
key: C# minor
style: cinematic
tempo: 60
time: 4/4

